  "summary_en": "State Comptroller audit of Israel's national AI preparedness (2018–2024). It finds no long-term national AI strategy, no integrating government body, low budget realization of the Telem program, declining international rankings, and delays on a Hebrew/Arabic language model. It recommends a comprehensive national program with clear responsibilities, budget and oversight.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Israel lacks a long-term national AI strategy and master implementation plan.",
   "No integrating government body leads the national AI program; the Telem structure is voluntary and without budgetary authority.",
   "Only about 40% of the first-phase NIS 550 million was realized; supercomputing only 11%.",
   "Israel fell in the Tortoise (5th to 9th) and Oxford readiness (20th to 30th) indices.",
   "Recommends a detailed national plan with milestones, budget, periodic assessment, and Prime Minister/NSC monitoring."
  ],
